<robot name="GEN3_URDF_V12" version="1.0">

  <!--
    Project-specific dual-arm mounting model. Each Gen3 7-DoF arm's joint
    types, limits, transforms, link inertials, and mesh geometry are aligned
    with Kinova's official ros_kortex v2.5.2 vision V12 URDF:
    kortex_description/arms/gen3/7dof/urdf/
    GEN3-7DOF-VISION_ARM_URDF_V12.urdf

    The shared `mount` root, fixed mounting transforms, dual-arm naming, and
    omission of camera frames are project-specific. URDF limits are model
    metadata; installed firmware/configured soft limits remain separate.

    ConfiguredTool_Link (right arm only) is also project-specific: it is
    NOT part of Kinova's stock arm geometry. It encodes the physical tool
    presently mounted on the right arm's flange, read from the robot itself
    via ControlConfig::GetToolConfiguration on 2026-08-05 (tools/
    print_tool_configuration.cpp): xyz 0 0 0.12 m, no rotation, mass
    0.831 kg, mass center 0 0 0.0473 m. This is a live robot SETTING, not a
    fixed property of the Gen3 arm — if the mounted tool ever changes,
    re-read GetToolConfiguration and update this offset, or FK will again
    diverge from the Kinova web dashboard's tool_pose the way it did before
    this was added.
  -->

  <!--
    MOUNTING BLOCK — GENERATED BY HAND FROM config/dual_arm_mounting.yaml.
    That YAML is the source of truth; these two joints must agree with it.
    tests/test_dual_arm_mounting.cpp enforces the agreement and fails the
    test step naming the offending number. Edit the YAML first.

    `mount` sits at the MIDPOINT of the two base_link origins, so each base
    is at [0, -+separation/2, 0] with roll -+tilt about mount X:

      separation 0.113415 m  ->  -+0.0567075 m along mount y
      tilt       1.2085 rad  =  -+69.2419 deg

    A URDF <origin> composes as Trans(xyz) then Rot(rpy), so one fixed joint
    per arm expresses this directly. (This replaced a two-joint
    rotate-then-translate chain through intermediate base_linktras /
    leftbase_linktras links, which placed the root 0.149614 m above the
    midpoint; the links carried no geometry and are gone.)
  -->
  <link name="mount"/>

  <joint name="right_base_mount" type="fixed">
    <origin rpy="1.2085 0 0" xyz="0 -0.0567075 0"/>
    <parent link="mount"/>
    <child link="base_link"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="base_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.000648 -0.000166 0.084487" rpy="0 0 0" />
      <mass value="1.697" />
      <inertia ixx="0.004622" ixy="9E-06" ixz="6E-05" iyy="0.004495" iyz="9E-06" izz="0.002079" />
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0" />
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://kortex_description/arms/gen3/7dof/meshes/base_link.STL" />
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="0.75294 0.75294 0.75294 1" />
